  "tagline": "Flash-optimized distributed key-value and document database for predictable sub-millisecond latency at scale.",
  "description": "Aerospike is a distributed NoSQL database built for real-time workloads that must keep sub-millisecond latency at millions of operations per second. Its hybrid memory architecture keeps indexes in RAM and data on NVMe SSDs, accessed directly rather than through a filesystem, which keeps clusters small and cheap relative to throughput. Records hold typed bins, including maps and lists usable as JSON documents. Version 8.0 added distributed multi-record ACID transactions, and 8.2 is the current release (September 2026). It is a staple of ad tech, fraud detection and payments, and is overkill for small apps.",
